# Anti-slop nuclear rules

## Principles

- Zero tolerance for redundancy.
- No unnecessary comments.
- No pointless wrappers.
- No excessive structural depth.

## Nuclear actions

- Remove any comment that is not a "why" with a ticket.
- Remove all duplicate functions or passive wrappers.
- Flatten structures: nesting must not exceed 2 levels.
- Split any function with multiple responsibilities.
- Delete files used only for organizing without logic.
- Rename generic variables (`data`, `info`, `result`) to semantic names.
- Remove unused imports without asking.

## Automatic delete criteria

If something has no explicit reason, is not used directly, does not provide immediate clarity, or is more complex than necessary, delete it.

## Red flags (immediate deletion)

- Syntax comments.
- Commented-out code.
- Redundant try/catch blocks.
- Files that only re-export.
- Empty or meaningless AI-style words ("robust", "seamless", etc.).
- Multiple returns without need.
- Empty catch blocks.
